=2 Walkthrough
* Speak with {n:Iruki-Waraki} who, during a cut-scene, asks you to inquire with his mentor, {n:Shamarhaan} about the situation.
* You can be any job from here on.
** **Note**: At this point, you can now commission {q:Dhima Polevhia|Dhima Polevhia|Dhima Polevhia} to craft three Artifact pieces. See her page for details.
* Travel to {z:Bastok Markets} and talk to {n:Shamarhaan} at (F-9) who gives a cut-scene and the key item {k:Valkeng's memory chip} from his own {p:Automaton}. He also tells you to retrieve an item from {z:Mount Zhayolm}.
* Travel to {z:Mount Zhayolm} and reach the position (L-8) to investigate the **???** located on a round steam vent on the ground to receive the key item {k:Toggle switch}.
** The easiest way to reach the location is via {p:Voidwatch} warp. From where you spawn head north and then turn left to move towards the south part of the map.
* After obtaining {k:Valkeng's memory chip} and the {k:Toggle switch}, find your way to {z:Talacca Cove} for a battle.
** The entrance is next to the {z:Caedarva Mire} {p:Home Point}. This will bring you straight in front of your destination.
*** If you dont have this yet {z:Nashmau} {p:Home Point} or {p:Survival Guide} then the west exit to {z:Caedarva Mire} is close also]].
* Examine the Rock Slab in the North-Western direction of the area for a cut-scene and to enter the battlefield to fight {n:Shamarhaan's|Shamarhaan} old military {p:Automaton}, {m:Valkeng}. The BCNM battle may include a party of up to 6 with a time limit of 30 minutes.
** {p:Trust Magic} is usable inside the battle.
* If underleveled/geared, this battle can prove to be very challenging for an unbalanced and low-number group.
** This fight is trivial for an ilevel 119 player to solo on any job.
* {m:Valkeng} is an {p:Automaton} type mob beginning as a {i:Harlequin Frame|Harlequin Frame|8224} and every 30 seconds, will change into a different frame depending on the grand total of damage types it has received during the battle. {m:Valkeng} will never return to its initial {i:Harlequin Frame|Harlequin Frame|8224}.
** If 50% or more of its damage taken has been from Melee attacks, it will change to its {i:Valoredge Frame|Valoredge Frame|8225} form.
** If 50% or more of its damage taken has been from Ranged attacks, it will change to its {i:Sharpshot Frame|Sharpshot Frame|8226} form.
** If 50% or more of its damage taken has been from Magic, it will change to its {i:Stormwaker Frame|Stormwaker Frame|8227} form.
* Each frame {m:Valkeng} changes to has significant stat and strategy changes.
** {i:Harlequin Frame|Harlequin Frame|8224} form:
*** Casts {s:Dia II}
*** Uses {p:Slapstick} weaponskill
*** Receives normal damage
** {i:Valoredge Frame|Valoredge Frame|8225} form:
*** Very fast attack rate
*** Very high {p:Accuracy} and {p:Attack}
*** Very high physical damage reduction
*** Uses {p:Chimera Ripper} and {p:String Clipper} weaponskills
** {i:Sharpshot Frame|Sharpshot Frame|8226} form:
*** Very high {p:Accuracy} and {p:Evasion}
*** Uses {p:Ranged Attacks|Ranged Attack} every 5 seconds
*** Uses {p:Slapstick} and {p:Arcuballista} weaponskills
*** Has low physical defense
** {i:Stormwaker Frame|Stormwaker Frame|8227} form:
*** Casts various high-level {s:Elemental Magic} every 10 seconds
*** Uses {p:Slapstick} weaponskill
*** Very high Magic Defense
*** Receives normal physical damage

* Upon defeating {m:Valkeng}, a cut-scene will occur. Choice of answer during will not affect any outcome.
* Return to {z:Bastok Markets} and speak to {n:Shamarhaan} for a cut-scene. Again, the answer to the question will not matter.
* Travel back to {p:Aht Urhgan Whitegate} to speak with {n:Iruki-Waraki} once again for a cut-scene.
* Travel to {z:Nashmau} and speak with {n:Sajhra} at (H-9) in the docks for another cut-scene.
* Return to {n:Iruki-Waraki} in {p:Aht Urhgan Whitegate} and speak with him for one last cut-scene and to receive your reward: {i:Puppetry Taj|Pup. Taj|15267}

=4 Artifact Commission
After receiving the quest Puppetmaster Blues, you may commission {p:Puppetmaster} {i:Artifact Armor} from {q:Dhima Polevhia|Dhima Polevhia|Dhima Polevhia}.
You may choose the order in which you receive the armor. You must wait until the next Vana'diel day to receive the piece you chose, and may commission a new piece immediately after the last piece was completed.
